ooking on with concern. In Frames 18-19, they are shown from behind, walking away from the scene, suggesting they are avoiding or escaping the situation.\n\n- **Interaction with the Teacher:** There is no positive interaction with any teacher figure. The only adult figure shown is a woman in a nurse or medical uniform (Frames 8-13) who is attending to a child on a stretcher. The children are not interacting with her in a friendly or engaged way; they are observing the situation with fear. The text in Frame 8, "okay kids, the substitute is on her way," suggests the arrival of a substitute teacher, but the children\'s reactions do not indicate any positive anticipation or welcome.\n\nIn summary, the children are showing clear negative reactions—fear, panic, and avoidance—towards the situation involving the substitute teacher and the medical emergency. There are no positive emotional cues or signs of engagement with the substitute teacher.'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-20 (20 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1490.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1491.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1492.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1493.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1494.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1495.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1496.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1497.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1498.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1499.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1500.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1501.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_1502.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lv