 the Teacher**:  \n   The children are not actively playing with toys or participating in structured activities with the teacher. Instead, they are gathered around him, suggesting a conversational or instructional moment. This indicates passive engagement rather than active play.\n\n6. **Signs of Positive or Negative Reactions**:  \n   There is no clear visual evidence of hatred, fear, or active dislike. No children are crying, running away, or showing aggression. While the children are not overtly expressing joy or adoration (e.g., smiling broadly, hugging, or jumping with excitement), their calm, attentive presence and lack of negative indicators suggest neutral-to-mildly-positive engagement.\n\n---\n\n**Conclusion**:  \nThe visual evidence does **not** support clear negative reactions (hate). The children’s behavior is consistent with **“don’t care” (option 3)** — they are present, not avoiding the teacher, but also not showing strong positive emotions like adoration or excitement. Their engagement is passive and neutral, typical of children in a new or unfamiliar adult-led situation.\n\n**Final Answer: 3**'}], 'formatted_responses': ['\n=== Batch 0-30 (30 frames) ===\nFrames: /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5650.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5651.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5652.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5653.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5654.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5655.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5656.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5657.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5658.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/frame_5659.jpg, /mnt/ssd/data/lvbench/videos_processed/uusf1qG_uZ4/frames/fra